BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Thespaceforart": "https://thespaceforart.com/event/tuesday-night-open-studio-figure-drawing-45/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:thespaceforart
X-SOURCE:The Space For Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261006T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261006T213000
DTSTAMP:20260928T214404Z
CREATED:20260928T214404Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260928T214404Z
UID:10563-1791313200-1791322200@thespaceforart.com
SUMMARY:Tuesday Night Open Studio Figure Drawing
DESCRIPTION:Every Tuesday\, 7 – 9:30 pm at the Space | All skill levels welcome \n*Cover art by Ling Chen. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTuesday night at The Space is your invitation to drop in\, find your creative flow\, and practice your drawing skills. \nEach week a different model – usually nude\, and sometimes clothed – serves as our muse as we pursue creative expression through observation and mark making. We challenge how we see and what we want to say\, observing the nuances of the human form\, its moods\, character\, and light — and do our best to capture something in the moment that tells a story. \nThis has become a supportive community of seekers\, artists\, experimenters\, and curious souls drawn together by the shared pursuit of capturing the living human form. Use the time to refine your skills\, experiment with different media\, and deepen your understanding of anatomy\, gesture\, and proportion. Challenge your process if you have one\, or begin to develop one if you don’t. Learn to truly see. \nEach session features a variety of poses\, from quick gesture sketches to longer\, more detailed studies. Whether you’re looking to sharpen your technical abilities\, loosen up your line work\, or simply enjoy the meditative experience of drawing from life\, this open studio is designed to support individual growth in a collaborative atmosphere. All skill levels are welcome – we’ve even had poets drop in and compose verses to the vibe in the room. \nBring your preferred supplies – charcoal\, graphite\, ink\, pastels\, and paint are all welcome. \nBasic drawing materials are available if you don’t have any\, and the shop has drawing pads and supplies for sale. No formal instruction is provided\, but peer feedback and self-guided exploration are always part of the mix. \nGood music. Good people. See you Tuesday. 7 – 9:30 pm at the Space. \nTickets are set at a capacity of 12\, but we accommodate up to 18 for those paying in cash. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n“The object isn’t to make art\, its to be in that wonderful state which makes art inevitable.” – Robert Henri
URL:https://thespaceforart.com/event/tuesday-night-open-studio-figure-drawing-45/
LOCATION:the Space\, 356 Bloomfield Ave\, Montclair\, New Jersey\, 07042
CATEGORIES:Art
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thespaceforart.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/20260820_220438-1-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Unioncong": "https://www.unioncong.org/event/union-cong-discusses-the-sum-of-us-guild-room/2026-10-06/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:unioncong
X-SOURCE:Union Congregational Church
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261006T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261006T203000
DTSTAMP:20261003T010258
CREATED:20260828T131203Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260828T131203Z
UID:10004940-1791313200-1791318600@www.unioncong.org
SUMMARY:Union Cong Discusses: The Sum of Us (Guild Room)
DESCRIPTION:The Racial Justice Ministry Team is sponsoring a 2-session book discussion of The Sum of Us: What Racism Costs Everyone and How We Can Prosper Together by Heather McGhee\, in advance of the townwide Open Book/Open Mind program: Heather McGhee in conversation with Michelle Alexander (free with registration) on October 13.  \nThe book traces the history of how some communities\, faced with integration\, chose instead to defund\, eliminate\, and ultimately privatize public goods such as public swimming pools. But there is a better\, more hope-filled way: to grow the pie to benefit everyone and collect the Solidarity Dividend.   \nJoin Union members and friends for pizza and discussion of key book topics (summary sheets available for download in advance) and personal reflection on September 29 and October 6 from 7 pm – 8:30 pm in the Main Building. Discussion topics will be different each week\, so please plan to attend one or both sessions! Please RSVP here so we can be sure to have enough pizza. This is an intergenerational event for Middle Schoolers through Adult.  \nMany of you already have a copy of the book. If you don’t yet have a copy\, feel free to pick one up (it’s available in both adult and young adult versions) from your local library or favorite book vendor or reach out to Ina Isobe (ina.isobe@gmail.com) for a church library copy.
URL:https://www.unioncong.org/event/union-cong-discusses-the-sum-of-us-guild-room/2026-10-06/
LOCATION:Guild Room
CATEGORIES:All Church Events,All Events,Featured Events,Justice & Community Engagement
END:VEVENT
