BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_racioppi
SUMMARY:Acolyte Training #2
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261011T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261011T120000
DTSTAMP:20261003T050240Z
UID:5bbru4m7od0mq64lh5g0ni1ujh@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261011T113000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260921T193029Z
DESCRIPTION:<span><span>Is your child sixth grade or older? Would s/he lik
 e to be <b>an acolyte</b>?<i> A what? </i>According to <a href="https://ww
 w.episcopalchurch.org/glossary/acolyte/" target="_blank">The Episcopal Chu
 rch website</a>\, an acolyte is defined as "</span></span><span>A general 
 term which covers not only servers\, torchbearers\, and lighters of candle
 s but also crucifers\, thurifers\, and banner-bearers."<br><br></span><spa
 n>At Holy Spirit Verona\, sixth to eighth grade students have a<b> Sunday 
 School class offered twice a month</b>. On the non-class Sundays\,<strong>
  sixth to 8th grade students </strong>are encouraged to be torchbearers\, 
 banner-bearers and second cross bearer at times on weeks when there is no 
 junior/high school Sunday School Class. And on the non-class Sundays\, <s
 trong>ninth to twelfth grade students</strong> can be lead cross bearers a
 t times if interested. Confirmation Students can use this time at "service
 " or "outreach hours."</span><br><span><br>We will host <b>two training se
 ssions</b> this fall for new acolytes -- attendance at ONE sessions is eno
 ugh\, but if your child wants to attend both that works too! <b>Meet at th
 e Ushers' Table in the Sanctuary at 11:30am</b> on either/both Sundays (<b
 >September 27 or/and October 11</b>). If you have any questions\, speak wi
 th Danielle Mueller or Father Jerry. </span>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260921T194908Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Church of the Holy Spirit Verona
END:VEVENT
