SUMMARY:Tuesday Open Studio Figure Drawing
DESCRIPTION:Every Tuesday\, 7 – 9:30 pm at the Space | All skill levels welcome \n*Cover art by Ling Chen. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTuesday night at The Space is your invitation to drop in\, find your creative flow\, and practice your drawing skills. \nEach week a different model – usually nude\, and sometimes clothed – serves as our muse as we pursue creative expression through observation and mark making. We challenge how we see and what we want to say\, observing the nuances of the human form\, its moods\, character\, and light — and do our best to capture something in the moment that tells a story. \nThis has become a supportive community of seekers\, artists\, experimenters\, and curious souls drawn together by the shared pursuit of capturing the living human form. Use the time to refine your skills\, experiment with different media\, and deepen your understanding of anatomy\, gesture\, and proportion. Challenge your process if you have one\, or begin to develop one if you don’t. Learn to truly see. \nEach session features a variety of poses\, from quick gesture sketches to longer\, more detailed studies. Whether you’re looking to sharpen your technical abilities\, loosen up your line work\, or simply enjoy the meditative experience of drawing from life\, this open studio is designed to support individual growth in a collaborative atmosphere. All skill levels are welcome – we’ve even had poets drop in and compose verses to the vibe in the room. \nBring your preferred supplies – charcoal\, graphite\, ink\, pastels\, and paint are all welcome. \nBasic drawing materials are available if you don’t have any\, and the shop has drawing pads and supplies for sale. No formal instruction is provided\, but peer feedback and self-guided exploration are always part of the mix. \nGood music. Good people. See you Tuesday. 7 – 9:30 pm at the Space. \nTickets are set at a capacity of 12\, but we accommodate up to 18 for those paying in cash. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n“The object isn’t to make art\, its to be in that wonderful state which makes art inevitable.” – Robert Henri
URL:https://thespaceforart.com/event/tuesday-open-studio-figure-drawing/
LOCATION:the Space\, 356 Bloomfield Ave\, Montclair\, New Jersey\, 07042
CATEGORIES:Art,Figure Drawing
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thespaceforart.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/20260820_220438-1-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
