X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Peakperfs": "https://www.peakperfs.org/event/classic-films-now-rocky/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:peakperfs
X-SOURCE:PEAK Performances at MSU
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T163000
DTSTAMP:20261002T212356
CREATED:20260719T165345Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260816T232538Z
UID:6018-1794146400-1794155400@www.peakperfs.org
SUMMARY:Classic Films Now: Rocky
DESCRIPTION:Run Time: 120 minutes\, recommended for ages 11+ \nA nation distrusts its institutions. News has become spectacle. Ordinary people fight to matter. Welcome to 1976. \nA club fighter from Philadelphia who moonlights as a collector for a local mobster gets a shot at the big time when the heavyweight champion of the world gives him chance to fight for the belt on America’s bicentennial. \n \nClassic Films Now brings major works of cinema back to the big screen\, films that not only defined their own time but continue to speak to ours. Each installment of the series gathers a group of landmark films curated around a theme\, period\, artist\, or movement\, inviting audiences to discover how the works connect with contemporary life. \nThis fall\, Classic Films Now kicks off with a three-film series devoted to 1976\, a remarkable year in American cinema and a revealing moment in the nation’s cultural imagination. Released in the shadow of Watergate\, Vietnam\, urban crisis\, and the Bicentennial\, All the President’s Men\, Network\, and Rocky offer three sharply different portraits of American life at a time of great transition and uncertainty. \nScreenings will be introduced and hosted by Rafer Guzmán. Rafer writes about movies\, music\, and popular culture for Newsday. He has been a film critic for WNYC\, a co-host of the independent podcast “Movie Therapy\,” and a staff writer at The Wall Street Journal.
URL:https://www.peakperfs.org/event/classic-films-now-rocky/
CATEGORIES:2026 - 2027
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.peakperfs.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/rock-peak-performances.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ics Kstx8Swyw669Kakgqa 6478083 Ics": "https://teamup.com/kstx8swyw669kakgqa/events/2167281732"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ics_kstx8swyw669kakgqa_6478083_ics
SUMMARY:Concert: An Afternoon of Klezmer
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261108T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261108T180000
DTSTAMP:20261002T220316Z
UID:TU2167281732
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261108T160000
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260911T204122Z
DESCRIPTION:**An Afternoon of Klezmer**  \nJoin us for a Sunday afternoon 
 of listening\, dancing\, and rejoicing with the Isle of Klezbos\, the accl
 aimed all-female klezmer ensemble. Described by New York Magazine as “cu
 tting-edge Klezmer\," this powerhouse sextet brings a beautiful balance of
  tradition and modern flair. Their music spans an incredible variety of st
 yles from neo-traditional folk dance and Yiddish swing to unexpected rhyth
 ms like reggae\, retro tango\, and Latin grooves.  \n**Sun\, Nov 8\, 2026\
 , 4:00pm**\n\n- Ticket Details to come\n\n**Purchase Tickets Here:** (link
  to come)  \n  \n***Sponsored by the Eric Singer Charitable Fund and Congr
 egation Shomrei Emunah***\n\n\\#ejcc\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260930T181452Z
LOCATION:Social Hall
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL;VALUE=URI:https://teamup.com/kstx8swyw669kakgqa/events/2167281732
X-SOURCE:Congregation Shomrei Emunah
X-TEAMUP-ROOM:Social Hall
END:VEVENT
